---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="Infrastructure inventory for the homelab"><section class="wrap hero"><div><div class="eyebrow">RackChief · V1.0.0</div><h1>Know what’s in your rack.</h1><p>Infrastructure inventory and project planning for the homelab. Track hardware, networking, racks, spare components, and the work that keeps everything moving.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="/docs/">Get started →</a><a class="button secondary" href="https://github.com/RackChief/RackChief">View on GitHub ↗</a></div></div><div class="panel"><div class="eyebrow">Your infrastructure, mapped</div><h2>Inventory that thinks in relationships.</h2><p class="muted">Assets connect to locations, racks, interfaces, ports, projects, and each other.</p><div class="rack">{Array.from({length:18}).map((_,i)=><span style={`opacity:${.45+(i%4)*.15}`}></span>)}</div></div></section><section class="wrap section"><div class="grid"><div class="card"><div class="icon">▣</div><h3>Inventory</h3><p class="muted">Assets, hardware, components, locations, and rack placements.</p></div><div class="card"><div class="icon">⌁</div><h3>Networking</h3><p class="muted">Interfaces, IP addresses, physical ports, and connections.</p></div><div class="card"><div class="icon">◌</div><h3>Planning</h3><p class="muted">Projects, purchases, work items, and planned upgrades.</p></div></div></section></Layout>
